#: videomass/vdms_panels/audio_encoders/acodecs.py:1014
msgid "PEAK level normalization, which will produce a maximum peak level equal to the set target level."
msgstr ""

#: videomass/vdms_panels/audio_encoders/acodecs.py:1018
msgid "RMS-based normalization, which according to mean volume calculates the amount of gain to reach same average power signal."
msgstr ""

#: videomass/vdms_panels/audio_encoders/acodecs.py:1023
msgid ""
"Loudnorm normalization. Normalizes the perceived loudness using the \"loudnorm\" filter, which implements the EBU R128 algorithm.\n"
"Ideal for live normalization. It produces worse results than the High-quality two-pass Loudnorm normalization, but is faster."
msgstr ""

#: videomass/vdms_panels/audio_encoders/acodecs.py:1031
msgid ""
"High-quality two-pass Loudnorm normalization. Normalizes the perceived loudness using the \"loudnorm\" filter, which implements\n"
"the EBU R128 algorithm. Ideal for postprocessing."
msgstr ""

#: videomass/vdms_panels/audio_encoders/acodecs.py:1145
msgid ""
"Listen to how each audio normalization filter sounds by clicking the Play/Stop button in the Timeline (CTRL+T).\n"
"\n"
"If a video file has multiple audio streams (tracks)—for example, audio in different languages—you can choose the specific stream you want, apply normalization to it, and hear the result.\n"
"\n"
"You can also test audio normalization in advance on standalone audio files from your collection before starting the conversion."
msgstr ""

